# ---- Trend monitor durable state (may hold tenant-scoped signals — never commit) ----
.trend-monitor/
# ---- Browser-walk artefacts (Playwright MCP) ----
# Every acceptance walk writes accessibility snapshots and console logs here.
# They are DIAGNOSIS, not evidence: a snapshot can contain a creator's own draft
# text and a console log can contain a request URL, and the vendor-acceptance
# runbook's rule 6 keeps both out of the evidence pack. What a walk PROVED
# belongs in its report card, in the operator's own words.
# Added 2026-09-04 by slice 8c's walk, alongside `respin/.tmp/` — the same class
# the round-1 code review raised as C14: this slice is entirely uncommitted, so
# a `git add -A` is the hazard, and an artefact directory nobody ignored is one
# the next walk recreates.
.playwright-mcp/
# ---- Cutdown job working directories (real creator footage + campaign data — never commit) ----
# `work/` holds ingested source media, proxies, renders and campaign exports for real
# jobs. Two independent reasons it can never be tracked: the media is licensed creator
# footage whose rights records live beside it (golden rule 3 / rights invariant), and the
# campaign exports (`comments.json`, `posts.json`) carry third-party personal data. It is
# also ~200 MB per campaign. The evidence that a job RAN belongs in `cutdown/docs/` and in
# the ContentPackage record — never the media itself.
work/
# ---- Editor / OS ----
.vs/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# ---- Local env / secrets (golden rule 2) ----
*.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# ---- Codebase map (generated, not tracked) ----
.codebase-map/
# ---- Playwright MCP (generated browser session artifacts, not tracked) ----
.playwright-mcp/
.gstack/
# ---- Machine-local caches and scratch (never useful in a clone) ----
# Codex sandbox scratch (node compile cache, tsx cache) and pnpm's
# content-addressable store. Both are rebuilt on demand, and both showed up in
# every `git status` — which is how a real change gets lost in the noise.
.codex-tmp/
.pnpm-store/
# Chromium DNS warnings left behind by a browser walk.
debug.log
